{"abstract":"There is an abundance of commercial and open-source eye trackers available for researchers interested in gaze and eye movements. Which aspects should be considered when choosing an eye tracker? The paper describes what distinguishes different types of eye trackers, their suitability for different types of research questions, and highlights questions researchers should ask themselves to make an informed choice.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798531"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye Movement","Eye tracking","Gaze direction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fundamentals of eye tracking part 000000000003 how to choose an eye tracker the fundamentals of eye tracking part 000000000003 how to choose an eye tracker","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-024-02587-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798531","identifier":[{"id":"85216608284","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5cb1ce39-4af1-4052-8720-aee936bd1882"],"keyword":["Choosing","Eye Movement","Eye tracking","Gaze direction"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-835AB79DC32F4CE9F3CFF5EEC61D6610"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-024-02587-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, BSc in Software Development","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3758/s13428-024-02587-x","issn":["1554351X","15543528"],"issn_org":["1554351X"],"issue":"67","journal":"Behavior Research Methods","publisher":"Psychonomic Society, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Behavior Research Methods","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216608284"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5cb1ce39-4af1-4052-8720-aee936bd1882"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The fundamentals of eye tracking part 3: How to choose an eye tracker : The fundamentals of eye tracking part 3: How to choose an eye tracker","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798531","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Researchers using eye tracking are heavily dependent on software and hardware tools to perform their studies, from recording eye tracking data and visualizing it, to processing and analyzing it. This article provides an overview of available tools for research using eye trackers and discusses considerations to make when choosing which tools to adopt for one’s study.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Niehorster, Diederick C.","Nyström, Marcus","Hessels, Roy S","Andersson, Richard","Benjamins, Jeroen S.","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Hooge, Ignace"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789542"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Tobii AB","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Eye tracking","Programming","Tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the fundamentals of eye tracking part 000000000004 tools for conducting an eye tracking study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-024-02529-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789542","identifier":[{"id":"85214364007","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-15d9f9fd-ec21-496e-8901-c49c7f69758b"],"keyword":["Eye tracking Software","Hardware and","Programming","Tools","eye tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1F35C39992C42DDAAE9AD9FC50989539"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3758/s13428-024-02529-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund Univ