{"abstract":"This paper highlights the complexity of creating a universal, cross-cultural Hand Gesture Recognition (HGR) vocabulary for global products and systems where worldwide users interact by sharing the same system or space. We revisit the concept of an idealistic universal HGR vocabulary for cross-cultural users and systems that suit all users and present potential development challenges by reviewing the hand gesture taxonomy, lexical, vocabulary, and the current design methods. The analysis emphasizes the importance of creating a cohesive movement towards standardizing HGR vocabulary for innovative products and services that accommodate cultural diversity and converge for a universal agreement at some point.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Munzlinger, Elizabete","Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Vucurevich, Ted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798570"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","GN Audio USA Inc."],"keyword":["Design methods","Human Computer Interaction","Taxonomy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"universal hand gesture interaction vocabulary for cross cultural users challenges and approaches","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85196308948","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798570","identifier":[{"id":"85196308948","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fab178d8-90f9-4175-8fdf-7e9bf7726bee"],"keyword":["Cross-Cultural Users","Design Methods","Global Products and Systems","Global Users","Hand Gesture Interaction","Human-Computer Interaction","Taxonomy","Universal Vocabulary"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1AD82E535045851C20F2A36A21244940"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["GN Audio A/S (Jabra)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"gn audio usa inc","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"GN Audio USA Inc.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elizabete","key":"munzlingerpau","last":"Munzlinger","locid":"4398dfd4-2627-4dbb-9ef1-de133b87f57f","name":"Munzlinger, Elizabete","orcid":"0009-0005-1202-9577","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabricio","key":"batistanarcizopau","last":"Batista Narcizo","name":"Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ted","key":"vucurevichpau","last":"Vucurevich","name":"Vucurevich, Ted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephanidis","key":"cpedh","last":"C.","name":"C., Stephanidis","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antona","key":"mpedh","last":"M.","name":"M., Antona","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ntoa","key":"spedh","last":"S.","name":"S., Ntoa","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Salvendy","key":"gpedh","last":"G","name":"G, Salvendy","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-61932-8_8","eisbn":["9783031619328"],"isbn":["9783031619311"],"issn":["18650929"],"pages":"56-69","publisher":"Springer","series":"Communications in Computer and Information Science","status":"p","title":"26th International Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"2114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196308948"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","gn audio a/s (jabra)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fab178d8-90f9-4175-8fdf-7e9bf7726bee"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Universal Hand Gesture Interaction Vocabulary for Cross-Cultural Users: Challenges and Approaches","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798570","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Autism Spectrum Condition (ASC) is characterised by difficulties in social communication and interaction, which may pose significant challenges to daily functioning throughout life. While current diagnostic methods for ASC often rely on measures based on subjective reports, there is a growing need for objective, quantifiable measures to support current clinical assessment of ASC. Eye-tracking technology records eye and gaze movements in real time and provides a direct and objective method for assessing social attention. Integrating eye-tracking within virtual reality (VR) environments presents a novel approach for capturing gaze behaviour in dynamic, ecologically valid social scenarios. This study aims to investigate whether VR-based eye information can reveal group differences in gaze behaviour between autistic adults and neurotypical controls in simulated social interactions. Methods This case-control study will include 140 adults diagnosed with ASC and 50 neurotypical controls, matched by age and gender. Participants will engage in six VR-based social scenarios, which vary in social complexity and the presence of non-social distractors. Eye information will be measured using eye-tracking technology integrated into a head-mounted display. Gaze behaviour will be analysed through fixation-based metrics on parameters including number of fixations, mean fixation time, and dwell time, on predetermined Areas of Interest. Analysis Statistical analyses will assess between-group differences in gaze behaviour as well as correlations between gaze metrics and clinical measures of social functioning, social cognition and symptom severity. Discussion This study utilises VR-based eye-tracking to investigate novel paradigms for assessing gaze behaviour in ASC in immersive, interactive environments and aims to advance the current understanding of visual social attention in ASC. Positive outcomes from this study may support further research into VR- based eye-tracking to supplement existing clinical assessment methods.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","C. E. Jeppesen, Alberte","Andresen, Johannes","Parvaiz, Rizwan","Clemmensen, Lars","Møllegaard Jepsen, Jens Richardt","Glenthøj, Louise B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789575"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol for the eyedentify project an examination of gaze behaviour in autistic adults using a virtual reality based paradigm study protocol for the eyedentify project an examination of gaze behaviour in autistic adults using a virtual reality based paradigm","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.12.14.24319035","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789575","ids":["itu-e21b8d51-1577-45ad-a888-f33394524c6b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-36ABFE3F7DD1480632D4D00D22F8282D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1101/2024.12.14.24319035","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, BSc in Software Development","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Region Hovedstaden","Region Hovedstadens Psykiatri"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberte","key":"cejeppesenpau","last":"C. E. Jeppesen","name":"C. E. Jeppesen, Alberte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Johannes","key":"andresenpau","last":"Andresen","name":"Andresen, Johannes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rizwan","key":"parvaizpau","last":"Parvaiz","name":"Parvaiz, Rizwan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","name":"Clemmensen, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Richardt","key":"møllegaardjepsenpau","last":"Møllegaard Jepsen","name":"Møllegaard Jepsen, Jens Richardt","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise B","key":"glenthøjpau","last":"Glenthøj","name":"Glenthøj, Louise B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/2024.12.14.24319035","issn":["30672007"],"journal":"medRxiv","status":"p","title":"medRxiv","title_org":"MEdRxiv","volume":"medRxiv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e21b8d51-1577-45ad-a888-f33394524c6b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Study protocol for the EYEdentify project: An examination of gaze behaviour in autistic adults using a virtual reality-based paradigm : Study protocol for the EYEdentify project: An examination of gaze behaviour in autistic adults using a virtual reality-based paradigm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789575","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents, RallyTemPose, a transformer encoder-decoder model for predicting future badminton strokes based on previous rally actions. The model uses court position, skeleton poses, and player-specific embeddings to learn stroke and player-specific latent representations in a spatiotemporal encoder module. The representations are then used to condition the subsequent strokes in a decoder module through rally-aware fusion blocks, which provide additional relevant strategic and technical considerations to make more informed predictions. RallyTemPose shows improved forecasting accuracy compared to traditional sequential methods on two real-world badminton datasets. The performance boost can also be attributed to the inclusion of improved stroke embeddings extracted from the latent representation of a pre-trained large-language model subjected to detailed text descriptions of stroke descriptions. In the discussion, the latent representations learned by the encoder module show useful properties regarding player analysis and comparisons. The code can be found at: This https url.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Graßhof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786364"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-18","place":"Seattle, WA, USA","start":"2024-06-17","title":"2024 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer vision","Conferences","Data models","Predictive models","Skeleton","Spatiotemporal phenomena","Transformers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a stroke of genius predicting the next move in badminton","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-786364","identifier":[{"id":"85206465133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d6976834-1abf-4b08-802c-345f77a4891c"],"keyword":["Computer vision","Conferences","Data models","Predictive models","Skeleton","Spatiotemporal phenomena","Transformers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-79706F66D6C1EFA9D47A0A01554C70CD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, ExerciseTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","name":"Ibh, Magnus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","name":"Graßhof, Stella","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","locid":"2fa369c5-96e8-43bb-8c9d-1331827e6802","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","orcid":"0000-0002-2164-234X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cvprw63382.2024.00342","eisbn":["9798350365474"],"isbn":["9798350365481"],"issn":["21607516"],"pages":"3376-3385","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","series":"IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops","status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206465133"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d6976834-1abf-4b08-802c-345f77a4891c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A stroke of genius : Predicting the next move in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786364","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a transformer encoder-decoder model for predicting future badminton strokes based on previous rally actions. The model uses court position skeleton poses and player-specific embeddings to learn stroke and player-specific latent representations in a spatiotemporal encoder module. The representations are then used to condition the subsequent strokes in a decoder module through rally-aware fusion blocks which provide additional relevant strategic and technical considerations to make more informed predictions. RallyTemPose shows improved forecasting accuracy compared to traditional sequential methods on two real-world badminton datasets. The performance boost can also be attributed to the inclusion of improved stroke embeddings extracted from the latent representation of a pre-trained large-language model subjected to detailed text descriptions of stroke descriptions. In the discussion the latent representations learned by the encoder module show useful properties regarding player analysis and comparisons.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764505"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Badminton","Transformer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a stroke of genius predicting the next move in badminton","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/html/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764505","identifier":[{"id":"85206465133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-467a45c0-0c66-4182-aa1f-8ac89dc0bac7"],"keyword":["badminton","transformer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-65CC6E1FEDAE3F23B6010B4306B1B067"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/html/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.html","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024W/CVsports/papers/Ibh_A_Stroke_of_Genius_Predicting_the_Next_Move_in_Badminton_CVPRW_2024_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","locid":"91d18624-3489-48a8-834d-8737581b8ff2","name":"Ibh, Magnus","orcid":"0009-0002-0334-4151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"3376-3385","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR) Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-467a45c0-0c66-4182-aa1f-8ac89dc0bac7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A stroke of genius: Predicting the next move in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764505","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents TemPose, a novel skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition to improve understanding of the detailed player actions in badminton. The model utilizes multiple temporal and interaction layers to capture variable-length multi-person human actions while minimizing reliance on non-human visual context. TemPose is evaluated on two fine-grained badminton datasets, where it significantly outperforms other baseline models by incorporating additional input streams, such as the shuttlecock position, into the temporal transformer layers of the model. Additionally, TemPose demonstrates great versatility by achieving competitive results compared to other state-of-the-art skeleton-based models on the large-scale action recognition benchmark NTU RGB+D. Experiments are conducted to explore how different model parameter configurations affect TemPose's performance. Additionally, a qualitative analysis of the temporal attention maps suggests that the model learns to prioritize frames of specific poses relevant to different actions while formulating an intuition of each individual's importance in the sequences. Overall, TemPose is an intuitive and versatile architecture that has the potential to be further developed and incorporated into other methods for managing human motion in sports with state-of-the-art results.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ibh, Magnus","Grasshof, Stella","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Madeleine, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718893"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fine grained action recognition","Human motion in sports","Skeleton based motion recognition","Temporal attention maps","Transformer model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tempose a new skeleton based transformer model designed for fine grained motion recognition in badminton","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753157/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718893","ids":["itu-904a4314-ec77-4601-b2d6-5809a2b83adc"],"keyword":["Fine-grained action recognition","Human motion in sports","Skeleton-based motion recognition","Temporal attention maps","Transformer model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1AE0EBB2641BB0CE1B9C0217967E75E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753157/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2023W/CVSports/papers/Ibh_TemPose_A_New_Skeleton-Based_Transformer_Model_Designed_for_Fine-Grained_Motion_CVPRW_2023_paper.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"ibhpau","last":"Ibh","locid":"91d18624-3489-48a8-834d-8737581b8ff2","name":"Ibh, Magnus","orcid":"0009-0002-0334-4151","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"grasshofpau","last":"Grasshof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pascal","key":"madeleinepau","last":"Madeleine","name":"Madeleine, Pascal","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"2023 Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition Workshops (CVPRW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-904a4314-ec77-4601-b2d6-5809a2b83adc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"TemPose: a new skeleton-based transformer model designed for fine-grained motion recognition in badminton","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718893","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This study investigates the influence of the eye-camera location associated with the accuracy and precision of interpolation-based eye-tracking methods. Several factors can negatively influence gaze estimation methods when building a commercial or off-the-shelf eye tracker device, including the eye-camera location in uncalibrated setups. Our experiments show that the eye-camera location combined with the non-coplanarity of the eye plane deforms the eye feature distribution when the camera is far from the eye's optical axis. This paper proposes geometric transformation methods to reshape the eye feature distribution based on the virtual alignment of the eye-camera in the center of the eye's optical axis. The data analysis uses eye-tracking data from a simulated environment and an experiment with 83 volunteer participants (55 males and 28 females). We evaluate the improvements achieved with the proposed methods using Gaussian analysis, which defines a range for high-accuracy gaze estimation between −0.5º and +0.5º. Compared to traditional polynomial-based and homography-based gaze estimation methods, the proposed methods increase the number of gaze estimations in the high-accuracy range.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","dos Santos, Fernando Eustáquio Dantas","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384661"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Science and Technology of the Northern Minas Gerais"],"keyword":["Eye Tracker","Eye tracking","gaze mapping calibration","high accuracy gaze estimation","uncalibrated setup"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high accuracy gaze estimation for interpolation based eye tracking methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vision5030041","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384661","identifier":[{"id":"85115335033","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e64c8d92-7526-4010-9aeb-8bda444fe325"],"keyword":["eye tracker","eye-tracking","gaze-mapping calibration","high-accuracy gaze estimation","uncalibrated setup"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-420D3BAB0A4F04C02FE96866FE731A3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86233091/vision_05_00041.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vision5030041","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"br","key":"science and technology of the northern minas gerais","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Science and Technology of the Northern Minas Gerais","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabricio","key":"batistanarcizopau","last":"Batista Narcizo","name":"Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fernando Eustáquio Dantas","key":"dossantospau","last":"dos Santos","name":"dos Santos, Fernando Eustáquio Dantas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/vision5030041","issn":["24115150"],"issue":"3","journal":"Vision","pages":"1","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Vision","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115335033"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e64c8d92-7526-4010-9aeb-8bda444fe325"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"High-Accuracy Gaze Estimation for Interpolation-Based Eye-Tracking Methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384661","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We present a framework to model and evaluate obfuscation methods for removing sensitive information in eye-tracking. The focus is on preventing iris-pattern identification. Candidate methods have to be effective at removing information while retaining high utility for gaze estimation. We propose several obfuscation methods that drastically outperform existing ones. A stochastic grid-search is used to determine optimal method parameters and evaluate the model framework. Precise obfuscation and gaze effects are measured for selected parameters. Two attack scenarios are considered and evaluated. We show that large datasets are susceptible to probabilistic attacks, even with seemingly effective obfuscation methods. However, additional data is needed to more accurately access the probabilistic security.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Eskildsen, Anton Mølbjerg","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695287"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","title":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research & Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye tracking","Obfuscation","Privacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of iris obfuscation generalising eye information processes for privacy studies in eye tracking","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86037440/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695287","identifier":[{"id":"85107667898","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-baa5d995-0f21-430b-b589-86491fdd6599"],"keyword":["eye-tracking","obfuscation","privacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4B52656F6AA373AD4BDBDDDBB769EB3C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86037440/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton Mølbjerg","key":"eskildsenpau","last":"Eskildsen","name":"Eskildsen, Anton Mølbjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3448017.3457385","eisbn":["9781450383448"],"pages":"1-10","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Applications","title":"ETRA '21 Full Papers"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107667898"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-baa5d995-0f21-430b-b589-86491fdd6599"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of iris obfuscation : Generalising eye information processes for privacy studies in eye tracking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695287","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We propose to use unlabelled eye image data for domain adaptation of an iris segmentation network. Adaptation allows the model to be less reliant on its initial generality. This is beneficial due to the large variance exhibited by eye image data which makes training of robust models difficult. The method uses a label prior in conjunction with network predictions to produce pseudo-labels. These are used in place of ground-truth data to adapt a base model. A fully connected neural network performs the pixel-wise iris segmentation. The base model is trained on synthetic data and adapted to several existing datasets with real-world eye images. The adapted models improve the average pupil centre detection rates by 24% at a distance of 25 pixels. We argue that the proposed method, and domain adaptation in general, is an interesting direction for increasing robustness of eye feature detectors.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Eskildsen, Anton Mølbjerg","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383985"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","title":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research & Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Domain adaptation","Iris segmentation","Neural network","Pseudo labels","Unlabelled eye image data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"label likelihood maximisation adapting iris segmentation models using domain adaptation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3379155.3391327","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383985","identifier":[{"id":"85086181110","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b9be6481-9342-419b-8f43-8d8400bd2811"],"keyword":["Domain adaptation","Iris segmentation","Neural network","Pseudo-labels","Unlabelled eye image data"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-395BB1FC180F39E2FA6B4A8045228F90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85694624/Label_Likelihood_Maximisation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3379155.3391327","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anton Mølbjerg","key":"eskildsenpau","last":"Eskildsen","name":"Eskildsen, Anton Mølbjerg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3379155.3391327","pages":"1-9","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ETRA '20 Full Papers: ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086181110"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b9be6481-9342-419b-8f43-8d8400bd2811"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Label Likelihood Maximisation: Adapting iris segmentation models using domain adaptation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383985","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objectives Biathlon is a discipline that combines cross country skiing with rifle shooting. It demands high shooting accuracy and fast shooting times under increasing levels of physiological fatigue. Building on Vickers and Williams (2007), the current study aimed at scrutinizing the impact of physiological fatigue and gaze behavior on shooting performance in elite and sub-elite biathletes. Design Ten members of the German national senior team (elite) and 13 members of the German national junior team (sub-elite) participated in a performance test. They conducted a roller skiing test on a treadmill including four increasing intensity levels followed by shooting blocks of five shots in both prone and standing position. Methods Physiological measurements consisted of heart rate and blood lactate, shooting performance data included shooting accuracy and time. Eye movements were assessed, i.e. the duration of the final fixation, using a gun-mounted eye tracking system. Results Physiological fatigue systematically increased across intensity levels. There were no differences between elite and sub-elite biathletes in percentage shooting accuracy. However, elites needed shorter shooting times than sub-elites. Both groups showed increased range times with increased workload levels in prone and standing positions. Yet, there was no effect on shooting accuracy. Finally, analyses of a subset of data did not show any effect of final fixation duration on shooting accuracy. Conclusions Physiological fatigue seems to have no impact on shooting accuracy, but rather affects shooting times in expert biathletes. Furthermore, the duration of the final fixation does not seem to moderate shooting accuracy in elite biathletes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Heinrich, Amelie","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Cañal-Bruland, Rouwen","Stoll, Oliver"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730170"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg"],"keyword":["Athletes","Attention","Biathlon shooting","Expertise","Physiology","Vision"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of physiological fatigue and gaze behavior on shooting performance in elite and sub elite biathletes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsams.2020.02.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730170","identifier":[{"id":"85081344106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5a1c82ee-9a3c-4fa6-9cc6-460b481faeb4"],"keyword":["Athletes","Attention","Biathlon shooting","Expertise","Physiology","Vision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-036BDD7D92116C672066539481406040"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsams.2020.02.010","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"martin luther university halle wittenberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"friedrich schiller university jena","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich Schiller University Jena","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelie","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Amelie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rouwen","key":"cañalbrulandpau","last":"Cañal-Bruland","name":"Cañal-Bruland, Rouwen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"stollpau","last":"Stoll","name":"Stoll, Oliver","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jsams.2020.02.010","edition":"9","pages":"883-890","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Science and Medicine in Sport","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85081344106"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5a1c82ee-9a3c-4fa6-9cc6-460b481faeb4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Impact of physiological fatigue and gaze behavior on shooting performance in elite and sub-elite biathletes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730170","year":"2020","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Captivity may have adverse effects on captive great apes, as they spend much more of their time engaged in foraging and other activities in the wild. Enrichment interventions have the potential to alleviate the adverse effects of captivity by introducing novel stimuli. In orangutans (Pongo pygmaeus), interactive digital enrichment has proven effective at engaging users out of their own free will, in exchange for nothing but the experience. This article reports the results of scheduled visual enrichment in the form of “orangulas”—one-hour long videos of footage consisting mainly of open spaces in different environments, with which the pongid participant could engage at free will. The efficacy of the orangulas were measured with both behavioural and endocrine measurements, concluding that scheduled visual enrichment has the potential to improve the welfare of captive orangutans by providing novel stimuli in the context of largely stable environments.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Olvido Perea Garcia, Juan","Miani, Alessandro","Miani, Alessandro","Malmkvist, Jens","Hammer, Trine","Pertoldi, Cino","Pertoldi, Cino","Pertoldi, Cino","Kruse Nielsen, Rikke","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Bach, Lars A"],"cuid":["S03-091.18-672368"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["García, Juan Olvido Perea"],"keyword":["Cortisol","Ethogram","no rewards","orangutan","scheduled","visual enrichment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Aalborg Zoo"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"orangulas effect of scheduled visual enrichment on behavioral and endocrine aspects of a captive orangutan pongo pygmaeus","src":["aau","au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.19227/jzar.v8i1.416","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-091.18-672368","ids":["aau-7e088bb3-f6e3-46ff-a853-9ee68334d942","au-b2640688-788a-4bbf-bfb8-b31b382fd272","itu-e6bcbee3-31c2-45ec-9a7b-1b47ef1d8341"],"keyword":["cortisol","ethogram","no rewards","orangutan","scheduled","visual enrichment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-718AF31D8163EC10462BEF8951AA32B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84856790/416_Article_Text_3380_2_10_20200131_1_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/400743954/416_Article_Text_3380_2_10_20200131.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.19227/jzar.v8i1.416","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Interacting Minds Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Biodiversity and Evolutionary Biology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biology and Environmental Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Law, AAU Arctic"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Aalborg Zoo"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan Olvido Perea","key":"garcíajuanolvidopereapau","last":"García","locid":"a7de4d2e-fe13-4594-ad8d-6deb4c624a00","name":"García, Juan Olvido Perea","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alessandro","key":"mianialessandropau","last":"Miani","locid":"2c27f922-f23e-43dc-8bf8-3ab31201b4e2","name":"Miani, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0001-6610-3510","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aage Kristian Olsen","key":"alstrupaagekristianolsenpau","last":"Alstrup","locid":"fa66f5b8-0468-4e85-b570-969776c5ebde","name":"Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","orcid":"0000-0002-0084-9122","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cino","key":"pertoldicinopau","last":"Pertoldi","locid":"e7abb09d-5c83-4796-ac11-84934c2035bc","name":"Pertoldi, Cino","orcid":"0000-0002-4644-8981","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"hammertrinepau","last":"Hammer","name":"Hammer, Trine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Hammer","key":"jensentrinehammerpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"ba730a1d-cca4-4f6b-9f9e-8cf67f00a53a","name":"Jensen, Trine Hammer","orcid":"0000-0001-9048-5280","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"krusenielsenrikkepau","last":"Kruse Nielsen","name":"Kruse Nielsen, Rikke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Kruse","key":"nielsenrikkekrusepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Kruse","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"bachlarsapau","last":"A. Bach","locid":"1b51c7d9-5db3-4f47-b004-6b434918c836","name":"Bach, Lars A.","name_org":"A. Bach, Lars","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansendanwitznerpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.19227/jzar.v8i1.416","issn":["22147594"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Zoo and Aquarium research","pages":"67-72","publisher":"European Association of Zoos and Aquaria","status":"p","title":"Journal of Zoo and Aquarium research","title_org":"Journal of Zoo and Aquarium Research","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7e088bb3-f6e3-46ff-a853-9ee68334d942","au-b2640688-788a-4bbf-bfb8-b31b382fd272","itu-e6bcbee3-31c2-45ec-9a7b-1b47ef1d8341"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Orangulas : effect of scheduled visual enrichment on behavioral and endocrine aspects of a captive orangutan (Pongo pygmaeus)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.18-672368","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this chapter we consider why it is important to study eye movements in natural, real world settings and the practical considerations that need to be taken into account when collecting eye movement data in these situations. Conducting a study in a real world environment poses very different challenges than those present in laboratory-based settings. Variables are hard to control and this restricts the kinds of paradigms that can be employed. Thus, careful consideration of the research question and whether it is appropriate for real world study is a necessary first step. Mobile eye trackers are often the most obvious choice for studying eye movements in real world settings. There exists a range of mobile eye tracking systems available to buy, and researchers also build their own mobile eye trackers to solve particular issues. Selecting the right system is an important consideration for mobile eye tracking and in this chapter we will highlight some of the key choices that the researcher should consider when buying or building a mobile eye tracker. Care must be taken to ensure that the data collected are sufficiently reliable to address the research question. While the principles of eye tracking - how we detect features of the eye and use these to estimate where someone is looking - are very similar for all eye trackers, the challenges faced when collecting data in natural settings are far greater than those that face eye trackers in a controlled laboratory setting. We will consider the key threats that real world settings pose for collecting reliable eye tracking data in the hope that we not only raise awareness of these issues but also offer some suggestions for how these can be minimised or at least identified in the data. For those considering whether to run an eye tracking study in the real world, we hope that this chapter will help you as you consider your research questions and choices of mobile eye tracker. For those already committed to studying eye movement behaviour in a real world setting, we hope that our discussion of the problems and possible solutions to the challenges faced in such settings will help minimise data loss from the common challenges that we face when conducting mobile eye tracking studies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tatler, Ben","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Pelz, Jeff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382721"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Rochester Institute of Technology","University of Aberdeen"],"keyword":["Data reliability","Eye movements","Mobile eye tracking","Real world settings","Research challenges"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eye movement recordings in natural settings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382721","ids":["itu-60a83879-f48f-49c1-8edf-9eef03bc7cbd"],"keyword":["Data reliability","Eye movements","Mobile eye tracking","Real world settings","Research challenges"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-8EB9116AF3A07014EA78DE0C936CBE58"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of aberdeen","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Aberdeen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"rochester institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rochester Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"tatlerpau","last":"Tatler","name":"Tatler, Ben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeff","key":"pelzpau","last":"Pelz","name":"Pelz, Jeff","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-20085-5_13","eisbn":["9783030200855"],"isbn":["9783030200831"],"place":"Martin Reuter & Christian Montag","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"An introduction to the scientific foundations of eye movement research and its applications Editors: Christoph Klein &amp; Ulrich Ettinger","title":"Eye Movement Research. Studies in Neuroscience, Psychology and Behavioral Economics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-60a83879-f48f-49c1-8edf-9eef03bc7cbd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Eye movement recordings in natural settings","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382721","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The duration of the so-called \"Quiet Eye\" (QE) - the final fixation before the initiation of a critical movement - seems to be linked to better perceptual-motor performances in various domains. For instance, experts show longer QE durations when compared to their less skilled counterparts. The aim of this paper was to replicate and extend previous work on the QE [Vickers and Williams 2007] in elite biathletes in an ecologically valid environment. Specifically, we tested whether longer QE durations result in higher shooting accuracy. To this end, we developed a gun-mounted eye tracker as a means to obtain reliable gaze data without interfering with the athletes' performance routines. During regular training protocols we collected gaze and performance data of 9 members (age 19.8 ± 0.45) of the German national junior team. The results did not show a significant effect of QE duration on shooting performance. Based on our findings, we critically discuss various conceptual as well as methodological issues with the QE literature that need to be aligned in future research to resolve current inconsistencies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","Heinrich, Amelie","Cañal-Bruland, Rouwen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384949"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","title":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research & Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich Schiller University Jena","Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg"],"keyword":["Biathlon","Eye tracking","Quiet Eye"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aiming for the quiet eye in biathlon","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3314111.3319850","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384949","identifier":[{"id":"85069473405","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fa1e80dd-6bbc-441e-a5bc-352732cd1966"],"keyword":["Biathlon","Eye tracking","Quiet Eye"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-686BDEE910D623AE41BA5380038E03B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3314111.3319850","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103464746/ETRA2019_Oberhof.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84834277/3314111.3319850.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"martin luther university halle wittenberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"friedrich schiller university jena","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich Schiller University Jena","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Amelie","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Amelie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rouwen","key":"cañalbrulandpau","last":"Cañal-Bruland","name":"Cañal-Bruland, Rouwen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3314111.3319850","eisbn":["9781450367097"],"pages":"1-8","place":"European Conference on Eye Movements","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ETRA '19: Proceedings of the 11th ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research &amp; Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069473405"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fa1e80dd-6bbc-441e-a5bc-352732cd1966"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aiming for the quiet eye in biathlon","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384949","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The use of additional information (a.k.a. priors) to help the eye tracking process is presented as an alternative to compensate classical geometrical problems in head-mounted eye trackers. Priors can be obtained from several distinct sources, such as: sensors to collect information related to distance, location, luminance, movement, speed; information extracted directly from the scene camera; calibration of video capture devices and other components of the eye tracker; information collected from a totally controlled environment; among others. Thus, priors are used to improve the robustness of eye tracking in real applications, for example, (1) If the distance between the subject and the viewed target is known, it is possible to estimate subject’s current point of regard even when target moves in depth and suffers influence of parallax error; and (2) if the tridimensional angular rotation is known, it is possible to compensate the error induced by the head rotations using linear regression. Experiments with simulated eye tracking data and in real scenarios of elite sports have been showing that the use of priors to support the eye tracking systems help produce more accurate and precise gaze estimation specially for uncalibrated head-mounted setups.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","Ahmed, Zaheer","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381316"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-24","place":"Wuppertal, de","start":"2017-08-20","title":"19th European Conference on Eye Movements","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye tracking","Gaze estimation","Head Mounted Eye Trackers","Parallax error","Priors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using priors to compensate geometrical problems in head mounted eye trackers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381316","ids":["itu-03d76511-4d2f-49d5-bc78-b96ae887ed24"],"keyword":["Eye Tracking","Gaze Estimation","Head-Mounted Eye Trackers","Parallax Error","Priors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C3B70FA4214B346C88ACA801AE3E572B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabricio","key":"batistanarcizopau","last":"Batista Narcizo","name":"Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Zaheer","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","name":"Ahmed, Zaheer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-03d76511-4d2f-49d5-bc78-b96ae887ed24"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Priors to Compensate Geometrical Problems in Head-Mounted Eye Trackers","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381316","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Preprocessor directives (#ifdefs) are often used to implement compile-time variability, despite the critique that they increase complexity, hamper maintainability, and impair code comprehensibility. Previous studies have shown that the time of bug finding increases linearly with variability. However, little is known about the cognitive process of debugging programs with variability. We carry out an experiment to understand how developers debug programs with variability. We ask developers to debug programs with and without variability, while recording their eye movements using an eye tracker. The results indicate that debugging time increases for code fragments containing variability. Interestingly, debugging time also seems to increase for code fragments without variability in the proximity of fragments that do contain variability. The presence of variability correlates with increase in the number of gaze transitions between definitions and usages for fields and methods. Variability also appears to prolong the \"initial scan\" of the entire program that most developers initiate debugging with.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Melo, Jean","Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383662"],"event":{"acronym":"ICPC","end":"2017-05-23","place":"Buenos Aires, ar","start":"2017-05-22","title":"2017 IEEE/ACM 25th International Conference on Program Comprehension","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cognition","Complexity theory","Computer bugs","Debugging","Eye Tracker","Eye movements","Eye tracking","Games","Gaze tracking","Highly Configurable Systems","Human factors","Open source software","Preprocessor Directives","Preprocessors","Program compilers","Software maintenance","Tools","Tracking","Variability","code comprehensibility","code fragments","cognitive process","compile time variability","debugging time","gaze transitions","program debugging","software maintainability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variability through the eyes of the programmer","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82174194/20170329_camera_ready_icpc.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383662","identifier":[{"id":"85025177144","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a4084045-d9f6-4428-8d56-e1e4ca6ddadf"],"keyword":["Complexity theory","Computer bugs","Debugging","Eye Tracking","Games","Highly-Configurable Systems","Open source software","Preprocessors","Tools","Tracking","Variability","code comprehensibility","code fragments","cognition","cognitive process","compile-time variability","debugging time","eye movements","eye tracker","gaze tracking","gaze transitions","human factors","preprocessor directives","program compilers","program debugging","software maintainability","software maintenance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-336C9BE4F825B6A3EEB144DB50E54B16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82174194/20170329_camera_ready_icpc.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean","key":"melopau","last":"Melo","name":"Melo, Jean","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabricio","key":"batistanarcizopau","last":"Batista Narcizo","name":"Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icpc.2017.34","eisbn":["9781538605356"],"pages":"34-44","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2017 IEEE/ACM 25th International Conference on Program Comprehension (ICPC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025177144"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a4084045-d9f6-4428-8d56-e1e4ca6ddadf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Variability through the Eyes of the Programmer","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383662","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We investigate the gaze estimation error induced by pupil size changes using simulated data. We investigate the influence of pupil diameter changes on estimated gaze point error obtained by two gaze estimation models. Simulation data show that at wider viewing angles and at small eye-camera distances, error increases with increasing pupil sizes. The maximum error recorded for refracted pupil images is 2.4° of visual angle and 1.5° for non-refracted pupil projections.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ahmed, Zaheer","Mardanbegi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384002"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","title":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research & Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["image processing eye tracking gaze estimation pupildynamics human computer interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pupil center as a function of pupil diameter","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80927677/Pupil_Center_as_a_Function_of_Pupil_Diameter.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384002","identifier":[{"id":"84975303243","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bb40de6e-179d-4c30-9537-20e60c8a0587"],"keyword":["image processing, eye tracking, gaze estimation, pupildynamics, human computer interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D2A61689C11C39B61579104D797D285"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80927677/Pupil_Center_as_a_Function_of_Pupil_Diameter.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zaheer","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","name":"Ahmed, Zaheer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbegipau","last":"Mardanbegi","name":"Mardanbegi, Diako","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2857491.2857536","isbn":["9781450341257"],"pages":"283-286","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ETRA '16 Proceedings of the Ninth Biennial ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research &amp; Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84975303243"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bb40de6e-179d-4c30-9537-20e60c8a0587"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pupil Center as a Function of Pupil Diameter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384002","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A depth compensation model is presented as a novel approach to reduce the effects of parallax error for head-mounted eye trackers. The method can reduce the parallax error when the distance between the user and the target is prior known. The model is geometrically presented and its performance is tested in a totally controlled environment with aim to check the influences of eye tracker parameters and ocular biometric parameters on its behavior. We also present a gaze estimation method based on epipolar geometry for binocular eye tracking setups. The depth compensation model has shown very promising to the field of eye tracking. It can reduce 10 times less the influence of parallax error in multiple depth planes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382983"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCV","title":"International Conference on Computer Vision"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Binocular eye tracking","Controlled environment","Depth compensation","Epipolar geometry","Gaze estimation","Geometric modeling","Head Mounted Eye Trackers","Ocular biometric parameters","Parallax error","Tracking accuracy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"depth compensation model for gaze estimation in sport analysis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84961997641","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382983","identifier":[{"id":"84961997641","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-74424974-3962-4822-8d4c-620a163a96eb"],"keyword":["Binocular eye tracking","Controlled environment","Depth compensation","Epipolar geometry","Gaze estimation","Geometric modeling","Head-mounted eye trackers","Ocular biometric parameters","Parallax error","Tracking accuracy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB9179E83B3C151D1BFF23CC19183A9E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabricio","key":"batistanarcizopau","last":"Batista Narcizo","name":"Batista Narcizo, Fabricio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/iccvw.2015.107","pages":"788-795","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2015 IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision Workshop (ICCVW)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961997641"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-74424974-3962-4822-8d4c-620a163a96eb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Depth Compensation Model for Gaze Estimation in Sport Analysis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382983","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"A novel normalization principle for robust glint detection is presented. The method is based on geometric properties of corneal reflections and allows for simple and effective detection of glints even in the presence of several spurious and identically appearing reflections. The method is tested on both simulated and data obtained from web cameras. The proposed method is a possible direction towards making eye trackers more robust to challenging scenarios.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","Roholm, Lars","García Ferreiros, Iván"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383488"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","title":"ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research & Applications"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Corneal reflections","Eye tracking","Normalization principle","Robust glint detection","Web camera data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robust glint detection through homography normalization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/78917612/etra2014GlintNormalisation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383488","identifier":[{"id":"84899697603","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-976dc2b6-b7a1-4b6e-a272-0ddd5f6fcf1a"],"keyword":["Corneal reflections","Eye tracking","Normalization principle","Robust glint detection","Web camera data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB18B768DA15DABCEC73E0D2D04ADFE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/78917612/etra2014GlintNormalisation.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2578153.2578165","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://eye.itu.dk","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"roholmpau","last":"Roholm","name":"Roholm, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Iván","key":"garcíaferreirospau","last":"García Ferreiros","name":"García Ferreiros, Iván","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2578153.2578165","isbn":["9781450327510"],"pages":"91-94","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ETRA '14 Proceedings of the Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84899697603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-976dc2b6-b7a1-4b6e-a272-0ddd5f6fcf1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Robust glint detection through homography normalization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383488","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The reported size of microsaccades is considerably larger today compared to the initial era of microsaccade studies during the 1950s and 1960s. We investigate whether this increase in size is related to the fact that the eye-trackers of today measure different ocular structures than the older techniques, and that the movements of these structures may differ during a microsaccade. In addition, we explore the impact such differences have on subsequent analyzes of the eye-tracker signals. In Experiment I, the movement of the pupil as well as the first and fourth Purkinje reflections were extracted from series of eye images recorded during a fixation task. Results show that the different ocular structures produce different microsaccade signatures. In Experiment II, we found that microsaccade amplitudes computed with a common detection algorithm were larger compared to those reported by two human experts. The main reason was that the overshoots were not systematically detected by the algorithm and therefore not accurately accounted for. We conclude that one reason to why the reported size of microsaccades has increased is due to the larger overshoots produced by the modern pupil-based eye-trackers compared to the systems used in the classical studies, in combination with the lack of a systematic algorithmic treatment of the overshoot. We hope that awareness of these discrepancies in microsaccade dynamics across eye structures will lead to more generally accepted definitions of microsaccades.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","Nyström, Marcus","Andersson, Richard","Hooge, Ignace"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384159"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Dynamic overshoot","Event detection","Eye deformation","Eye tracking","Microsaccade","Ocular structure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"why have microsaccades become larger investigating eye deformations and detection algorithms","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.visres.2014.11.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384159","identifier":[{"id":"84919346251","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c50b4e96-1efd-4886-b844-fa0330168ad1"],"keyword":["Dynamic overshoot","Event detection","Eye deformation","Eye tracking","Microsaccade","Ocular structure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-159575F4B864D59DBDE999599E43DD0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25481631","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.visres.2014.11.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"nyströmpau","last":"Nyström","name":"Nyström, Marcus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"anderssonpau","last":"Andersson","name":"Andersson, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ignace","key":"hoogepau","last":"Hooge","name":"Hooge, Ignace","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.visres.2014.11.007","issn":["00426989","18785646"],"issn_org":["00426989"],"journal":"Vision Research","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Vision Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84953411357"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c50b4e96-1efd-4886-b844-fa0330168ad1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Why have microsaccades become larger? : Investigating eye deformations and detection algorithms.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384159","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"While the new generation of eyewear computers have increased expectations of a wearable computer, providing input to these devices is still challenging. Hand-held devices, voice commands, and hand gestures have already been explored to provide input to the wearable devices. In this paper, we examined using head and eye movements to point on a graphical user interface of a wearable computer. The performance of users in head and eye pointing has been compared with mouse pointing as a baseline method. The result of our experiment showed that the eye pointing is significantly faster than head or mouse pointing; however, our participants thought that the head pointing is more accurate and convenient.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jalaliniya, Shahram","Mardanbeigi, Diako","Pederson, Thomas","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384499"],"event":{"acronym":"BSN","title":"Wearable and Implantable Body Sensor Networks"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye pointing","Gaze tracking","Head mounted display","Head pointing","Head tracking","Wearable Computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"head and eye movement as pointing modalities for eyewear computers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ess.tu-darmstadt.de/gec14/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384499","identifier":[{"id":"84919429783","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-dbca1cc3-adfe-41ee-9791-f3802df5fa65"],"keyword":["Eye pointing","Gaze tracking","Head pointing","Head tracking","head-mounted display","wearable computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F4851A6552EB96AE15DE9D8182DF3CD4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ess.tu-darmstadt.de/gec14/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shahram","key":"jalaliniyapau","last":"Jalaliniya","name":"Jalaliniya, Shahram","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"pedersonpau","last":"Pederson","name":"Pederson, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781479961368"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2014 11th International Conference on Wearable and Implantable Body Sensor Networks Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dbca1cc3-adfe-41ee-9791-f3802df5fa65"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Head and eye movement as pointing modalities for eyewear computers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384499","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Professional human translation is necessary to meet high quality standards in industry and governmental agencies. Translators engage in multiple activities during their task, and there is a need to model their behavior, with the objective to understand and optimize the translation process. In recent years, user interfaces enabled us to record user events such as eye-movements or keystrokes. Although there have been insightful descriptive analysis of the translation process, there are multiple advantages in enabling quantitative inference. We present methods to classify sequences of fixations and keystrokes into activities and model translation sessions with the objective to recognize translator expertise. We show significant error reductions in the task of recognizing certified translators and their years of experience, and analyze the characterizing patterns.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Gómez, Pascual Martínez","Minocha, Akshay","Huang, Jin","Carl, Michael","Bangalore, Srinivas","Aizawa, Akiko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-294275"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","end":"2014-03-28","place":"Safety Harbor, FL, us","start":"2014-03-26","title":"2014 Symposium on Eye tracking Research &amp; Applications","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["India","Japan","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AT&T Labs Research","All Global Affiliations","Durham University","Language Technologies Research Centre - Hyderabad","University of Tokyo"],"keyword":["Translation process research"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recognition of translator expertise using sequences of fixations and keystrokes","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-294275","identifier":[{"id":"84899702910","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-c664f3ff-b312-4882-aa41-f0fbdf56ec29"],"keyword":["Expertise modeling","Translation process research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1DE88F4B957EA41A35508640F36F278"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"jp","key":"university of tokyo","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"University of Tokyo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"language technologies research centre hyderabad","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Language Technologies Research Centre - Hyderabad","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"durham university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Durham University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of International Business Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"at t labs research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"AT&T Labs Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pascual Martínez","key":"gómezpau","last":"Gómez","name":"Gómez, Pascual Martínez","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Akshay","key":"minochapau","last":"Minocha","name":"Minocha, Akshay","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Jin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"carlpau","last":"Carl","locid":"32f523e8-1067-4b0b-813c-c445f8cd6261","name":"Carl, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2815-0292","ran