{"abstract":"This paper presents a fully calibrated extended geometric approach for gaze estimation in three dimensions (3D). The methodology is based on a geometric approach utilising a fully calibrated binocular setup constructed as a head-mounted system. The approach is based on utilisation of two ordinary web-cameras for each eye and 6D magnetic sensors allowing free head movements in 3D. Evaluation of initial experiments indicate comparable results to current state-of-the-art on estimating gaze in 3D. Initial results show an RMS error of 39-50 mm in the depth dimension and even smaller in the horizontal and vertical dimensions regarding fixations. However, even though the workspace is limited, the fact that the system is designed as a head-mounted device, the workspace volume is relatively positioned to the pose of the device. Hence gaze can be estimated in 3D with relatively free head-movements with external reference to a world coordinate system and is therefore offering flexibility and movability within certain constraints.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lidegaard, Morten","Witzner Hansen, Dan","Krüger, Norbert"],"cuid":["S02-089.47-038255"],"event":{"acronym":"ETRA","end":"2014-03-28","place":"Safety Harbor, Florida, us","start":"2014-03-26","title":"Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Application","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["3D Head Mounted System","6D Magnetic Sensors","Binocular Setup","Eye tracking","Fully calibrated geometric approach","Gaze estimation","Geometric Approach","Three dimensional 3D gaze tracking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"head mounted device for point of gaze estimation in three dimensions","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/102756416/p83_lidegaard.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-089.47-038255","identifier":[{"id":"84899701590","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0e2bd049-18b4-40cd-b539-32558f96fc88","sdu-03ef38f2-3371-405f-86f2-79334c53e41a"],"keyword":["3D Head-Mounted System","6D Magnetic Sensors","Binocular Setup","Geometric Approach","eye tracking","fully calibrated geometric approach","gaze estimation","three dimensional (3D) gaze tracking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-30025C76670D186CB156F0A08BC509C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2578153.2578163&coll=DL&dl=ACM&CFID=336795619&CFTOKEN=89556302","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2578153.2578163","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/102756416/p83_lidegaard.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/2578153.2578163","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen",