{"abstract":"Augmented cognition applications must deal with the problem of how to exhibit information in an orderly, understandable, and timely fashion. Though context have been suggested to control the kind, amount, and timing of the information delivered, we argue that gaze can be a fundamental tool to reduce the amount of information and provide an appropriate mechanism for low and divided attention interaction. We claim that most current gaze interaction paradigms are not appropriate for wearable computing because they are not designed for divided attention. We have used principles suggested by the wearable computing community to develop a gaze supported augmented cognition application with three interaction modes. The application provides information of the person being looked at. The continuous mode updates information every time the user looks at a different face. The key activated discrete mode and the head gesture activated mode only update the information when the key is pressed or the gesture is performed. A prototype of the system is currently under development and it will be used to further investigate these claims.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Toshiaki Kurauchi, Andrew","Hitoshi Morimoto, Carlos","Mardanbeigi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384404"],"event":{"end":"2013-04-27","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2013-04-27","title":"CHI 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of São Paulo"],"keyword":["Gaze interaction","Wearable Computing","augmented cognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards wearable gaze supported augmented cognition","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://gaze-interaction.net/workshop-program","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384404","ids":["itu-d5026572-f0a6-415e-bae8-270f6ab1148d"],"keyword":["augmented cognition","gaze interaction","wearable computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-97BFDC7D2A608785F4BACBC7F2040FAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://gaze-interaction.net/workshop-program","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"br","key":"university of são paulo","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"University of São Paulo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"toshiakikurauchipau","last":"Toshiaki Kurauchi","name":"Toshiaki Kurauchi, Andrew","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos","key":"hitoshimorimotopau","last":"Hitoshi Morimoto","name":"Hitoshi Morimoto, Carlos","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d5026572-f0a6-415e-bae8-270f6ab1148d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Wearable Gaze Supported Augmented Cognition","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384404","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This position paper outlines a research program for the IxD Research Group at the IT University of Copenhagen. As such, it presents a range of questions addressing different corners of the question of time in IxD from the point of view of HCI, social interaction, material expressions, and software development. Our ongoing investigation of Interaction Design for a Good Life (http://itu.dk/IxDLab/) has uncovered a broad diversity of perspectives on how to unpack ‘a good life’ through research and design, and indeed what constitutes a good life to begin with. Through our investigations, time has surfaced as pivotal to our budding understanding of elements of a good life and a useful framing for future investigations. Time is also an important topic for interaction design, because it is at the core of interaction, the practice of design, and, in many ways, our use and relationships with technological artifacts. Here we present our initial thoughts on time-related research directions that we wish to pursue.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Froes, Isabel Cristina G.","Laaksolahti, Jarmo Matti","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Heyer, Clint","Kotamraju, Nalini Panchita","Malmborg, Lone","Nielsen, Lene","Pedersen, Jens","Shklovski, Irina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381690"],"event":{"end":"2013-05-02","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2013-04-27","title":"CHI 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Interaction design","Material Expressions","Social interaction","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"time interaction and design in support of a good life","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381690","ids":["itu-1c4ed4ff-4baa-4bed-8dce-959b82eaa3da"],"keyword":["Human-Computer Interaction","Interaction Design","Material Expressions","Social Interaction","Software Development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7FC736A29E6798FD824C01E45E089356"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel Cristina G.","key":"froespau","last":"Froes","name":"Froes, Isabel Cristina G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jarmo Matti","key":"laaksolahtipau","last":"Laaksolahti","name":"Laaksolahti, Jarmo Matti","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Clint","key":"heyerpau","last":"Heyer","name":"Heyer, Clint","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nalini Panchita","key":"kotamrajupau","last":"Kotamraju","name":"Kotamraju, Nalini Panchita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","name":"Shklovski, Irina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1c4ed4ff-4baa-4bed-8dce-959b82eaa3da"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Time, Interaction, and Design in Support of a Good Life","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381690","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we suggest using a new method for head gesture recognition in the automotive context. This method involves using only the eye tracker for measuring the head movements through the eye movements when the gaze point is fixed. It allows for identifying a wide range of head gestures that can be used as an alternative input in the multimodal interaction context. Two approaches are described for using this method for interaction with objects inside or outside the car. Some application examples are described where the discrete or continuous head movements in combination with the driver’s visual attention can be used for controlling the objects inside the car.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mardanbeigi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382724"],"event":{"acronym":"AutomotiveUI","end":"2012-10-19","place":"Portsmouth, us","start":"2012-10-17","title":"4th International Conference on Automotive User Interfaces and Interactive Vehicular Applications","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye tracking","Head Gesture Recognition","Multimodal interaction","automotive interaction","driver attention"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eye based head gestures for interaction in the car","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.auto-ui.org/12/docs/AutomotiveUI-2012-Adjunct-Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382724","ids":["itu-60c271e6-e1af-46d3-8015-63fe0cccb3d6"],"keyword":["automotive interaction","driver attention","eye tracking","head gesture recognition","multimodal interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B7B3509E32A9D77C9F9B492028784B4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.auto-ui.org/12/docs/AutomotiveUI-2012-Adjunct-Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781450317511"],"pages":"39-42","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"AutomotiveUI '12","title":"Proceedings of the 4th International Conference on Automotive User Interfaces and Interactive Vehicular Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-60c271e6-e1af-46d3-8015-63fe0cccb3d6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Eye-based head gestures for interaction in the car","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382724","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Research and applications of gaze interaction has mainly been conducted on a 2 dimensional surface (usually screens) for controlling a computer or controlling the movements of a robot. Emerging wearable and mobile technologies, such as google glasses may shift how gaze is used as an interactive modality if gaze trackers are embedded into the head- mounted devices. The domain of gaze-based interactive applications increases dramatically as interaction is no longer constrained to 2D displays. This paper proposes a general framework for gaze-based controlling a non- stationary robot (vehicle) as an example of a complex gaze-based task in environment. This paper discusses the possibilities and limitations of how gaze interaction can be performed for controlling vehicles not only using a remote gaze tracker but also in general challenging situations where the user and robot are mobile and the movements may be governed by several degrees of freedom (e.g. flying). A case study is also introduced where the mobile gaze tracker is used for controlling a Roomba vacuum cleaner.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mardanbeigi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383741"],"event":{"end":"2013-04-27","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2013-04-27","title":"CHI 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Craft","Driving","Eye tracking","Gaze based interaction","Head Gestures","Robot","Vehicle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gaze based controlling a vehicle","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/38425416/Gaze_based_controlling_a_vehicle.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383741","ids":["itu-aa9772f7-c03d-470a-b234-9d7c1e5e9c3d"],"keyword":["Gaze-based interaction","craft","driving","eye tracking","head- gestures","robot","vehicle"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6466B6697294D8F855B2BD97C63495C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/38425416/Gaze_based_controlling_a_vehicle.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-aa9772f7-c03d-470a-b234-9d7c1e5e9c3d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gaze-Based Controlling a Vehicle","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383741","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates the parallax error, which is a common problem of many video-based monocular mobile gaze trackers. The parallax error is defined and described using the epipolar geometry in a stereo camera setup. The main parameters that change the error are introduced and it is shown how each parameter affects the error. The optimum distribution of the error (magnitude and direction) in the field of view varies for different applications. However, the results can be used for finding the optimum parameters that are needed for designing a head-mounted gaze tracker. It has been shown that the difference between the visual and optical axes does not have a significant effect on the parallax error, and the epipolar geometry can be used for describing the parallax error in the HMGT.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mardanbeigi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381915"],"event":{"end":"2012-09-08","place":"Pittsburgh, us","start":"2012-09-05","title":"The 14th International Conference on Ubiquitous Computing","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Epipolar geometry","Head mounted gaze tracker","Mobile gaze tracker","Parallax error"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parallax error in the monocular head mounted eye trackers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/39146509/Parallax_error.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381915","identifier":[{"id":"84879487013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2bca4d1f-a217-4bbf-9023-312cbab2b51e"],"keyword":["Head-mounted gaze tracker","Mobile gaze tracker","Parallax error","epipolar geometry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B9E97B101023179C70D39C78153791B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/39146509/Parallax_error.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781450312240"],"pages":"689-694","status":"p","title":"UbiComp '12 Proceedings of the 2012 ACM Conference on Ubiquitous Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879487013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2bca4d1f-a217-4bbf-9023-312cbab2b51e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Parallax error in the monocular head-mounted eye trackers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381915","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
