Hansen, John Paulin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Auliki","key":"hyrskykaripau","last":"Hyrskykari","name":"Hyrskykari, Auliki","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kari-Jouko","key":"räihäpau","last":"Räihä","name":"Räihä, Kari-Jouko","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781613500989"],"pages":"365-376","publisher":"Idea Group Publishing","status":"p","subtitle":"Advances in Assistive Technologies","title":"Gaze Interaction and Applications of Eye Tracking:"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-02d56518-170f-485b-9adb-3aa3dea795e6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Conclusion and Look to the Future","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381298","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"A novel method for video-based head gesture recognition using eye information by an eye tracker has been proposed. The method uses a combination of gaze and eye movement to infer head gestures. Compared to other gesture-based methods a major advantage of the method is that the user keeps the gaze on the interaction object while interacting. This method has been implemented on a head-mounted eye tracker for detecting a set of predefined head gestures. The accuracy of the gesture classifier is evaluated and verified for gaze-based interaction in applications intended for both large public displays and small mobile phone screens. The user study shows that the method detects a set of defined gestures reliably.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Mardanbegi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Pederson, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382781"],"event":{"end":"2012-03-30","place":"Santa Barbara, CA, us","start":"2012-03-28","title":"Symposium: Eye Tracking Research &amp; Applications","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye Tracker","Gaze interaction","Gesture Classifier","Head Gesture Recognition","Head Mounted Devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eye based head gestures","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2168556.2168578","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382781","identifier":[{"id":"84862666923","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-64f951e6-36d3-4d75-aeec-42a8a3f071e3"],"keyword":["Eye Tracker","Gaze Interaction","Gesture Classifier","Head Gesture Recognition","Head-Mounted Devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80402DCCB82B39BD7D470918E88F01A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2168556.2168578","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbegipau","last":"Mardanbegi","name":"Mardanbegi, Diako","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"pedersonpau","last":"Pederson","name":"Pederson, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2168556.2168578","isbn":["9781450312219"],"pages":"139-146","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ETRA '12 Proceedings of the Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84862666923"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-64f951e6-36d3-4d75-aeec-42a8a3f071e3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Eye-based head gestures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382781","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Seamless mobile navigation will reinforce social inclusion of people with Mild Cognitive Impairment (MCI) and will lower their anxiety levels when mobile in their usual habitats as they have at hand a means to support them in cases such as where they lose their way or forget where they were going. We have continued development from existing studies of vibrotactile displays (Van Erp, 2007), for our first prototype of a wearable assistive navigation device that gives a range of sensitive haptic feedback as part of an intended larger project. The larger project will develop methods and technology that provide “companion navigators”, which are of significant importance for social inclusion for people with navigation problems (Hansen et al, 2009). In addition, we add the concept of PeerCare as developed by Riche & MacKay (2010) in order to create a system that enhances the ability of elderly peers to communicate with and care for each other (Hutchinson et al, 2003). We describe here our methods for observing participants operating in their homes and usual habitats in order to design for their specific needs and to build a scalable living lab method (Winthereik et al, 2009) for urban and regional environments. As the prototypes become more robust, the repertoire expands and the user group is enlarged meaning a triangulation of design and testing methods is required.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Morrison, Ann","Andersen, Hans Jørgen","Malmborg, Lone","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Knudsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-103046"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Assistive technology","Elderly","Independence","Methodology","Mobility","Social inclusion"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"methodology for designing implementing and evaluating assistive mobility technology to enable the social inclusion and independence needs of an ageing population","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61155214/paper4.docx","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-103046","ids":["aau-b6829f5e-7d85-491f-8a96-bb5956e8f38f"],"keyword":["Assistive Technology","Elderly","Independence","Methodology","Mobility","Social inclusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-402D448E5F0BD79C8CB458BC69878560"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/61155214/paper4.docx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Research Laboratory for Art and Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Mobility and Tracking Technologies","Urban Vibrations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Instituttet"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann","key":"morrisonpau","last":"Morrison","locid":"c12a0005-5067-49e6-b979-902982ca88aa","name":"Morrison, Ann","orcid":"0000-0002-4005-4877","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Jørgen","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7ba27faa-e069-404b-8502-76309dad24a3","name":"Andersen, Hans Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-0940-0698","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"malmborgpau","last":"Malmborg","name":"Malmborg, Lone","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"40a6f0a3-0277-453c-9cb5-29eb248feb12","name":"Knudsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-8206-5638","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Undetermined","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b6829f5e-7d85-491f-8a96-bb5956e8f38f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Methodology for designing, implementing and evaluating assistive mobility technology to enable the social inclusion and independence needs of an ageing population","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-103046","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Head-mounted eye trackers can be used for mobile interaction as well as gaze estimation purposes. This paper presents a method that enables the user to interact with any planar digital display in a 3D environment using a head-mounted eye tracker. An effective method for identifying the screens in the field of view of the user is also presented which can be applied in a general scenario in which multiple users can interact with multiple screens. A particular application of using this technique is implemented in a home environment with two big screens and a mobile phone. In this application a user was able to interact with these screens using a wireless head-mounted eye tracker.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mardanbeigi, Diako","Hansen, Dan Witzner"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381761"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D environment","Digital display interaction","Gaze estimation","Head mounted eye tracker","Mobile interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobile gaze based screen interaction in 000000000003d environments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79960194825","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381761","identifier":[{"id":"79960194825","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-21208ecf-d58d-4dd2-9224-bef80c758a56"],"keyword":["- 3D environment","- Digital display interaction","- Gaze estimation","- Head-mounted eye tracker","- Mobile interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A443A27B952A7A8E908362C132344AB8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/1983302.1983304","isbn":["9781450306805"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NGCA 2011. Proceedings of the 1st Conference on Novel Gaze-Controlled Applications"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960194825"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-21208ecf-d58d-4dd2-9224-bef80c758a56"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mobile gaze-based screen interaction in 3D environments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381761","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates how eye tracking and gaze estimation can help create better mixedreality personal computing systems involving both physical (real world) and virtual (digital) objects. The role of gaze is discussed in the light of the situative space model (SSM) determining the set of objects (physical and virtual) which a given human agent can perceive, and act on, in any given moment in time. The analysis and discussion results in ideas for how to extend the SSM model in order to better incorporate the role of gaze in everyday human activities, and for taking advantage of emerging mobile eye tracking technology.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pederson, Thomas","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Mardanbeigi, Diako"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730200"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gaze tracking","Interaction paradigm"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigations of the role of gaze in mixed reality personal computing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103254523/PedersonEtAl_IUI2011.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730200","ids":["itu-e6fd2769-ef56-4742-8b3f-5bb75e27e708"],"keyword":["Gaze tracking","Interaction paradigm"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D9CC3205C4221844BAB1BA91EF605574"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103254523/PedersonEtAl_IUI2011.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"pedersonpau","last":"Pederson","name":"Pederson, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan","key":"witznerhansenpau","last":"Witzner Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","name_org":"Witzner Hansen, Dan","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbeigipau","last":"Mardanbeigi","name":"Mardanbeigi, Diako","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"67-70","status":"p","subtitle":"IUI'2011","title":"IUI '11: Proceedings of the 16th international conference on Intelligent user interfaces"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e6fd2769-ef56-4742-8b3f-5bb75e27e708"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigations of the Role of Gaze in Mixed-Reality Personal Computing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730200","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces the concept of using gaze as a sole modality for fully controlling player characters of fast-paced action computer games. A user experiment is devised to collect gaze and gameplay data from subjects playing a version of the popular Super Mario Bros platform game. The initial analysis shows that there is a rather limited grid around Mario where the efficient player focuses her attention the most while playing the game. The useful grid as we name it, projects the amount of meaningful visual information a designer should use towards creating successful player character controllers with the use of artificial intelligence for a platform game like Super Mario. Information about the eyes' position on the screen and the state of the game are utilized as inputs of an artificial neural network, which is trained to approximate which keyboard action is to be performed at each game step. Results yield a prediction accuracy of over 83% on unseen data samples and show promise towards the development of eye-controlled fast-paced platform games. Derived neural network players are intended to be used as assistive technology tools for the digital entertainment of people with motor disabilities.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Muñoz, Jorge","Yannakakis, Georgios N.","Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Gutierrez, German","Sanchis, Araceli"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382361"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game AI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards gaze controlled platform games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIG.2011.6031988","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382361","identifier":[{"id":"80054013729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-494d4082-cae2-48c3-a993-7381c219cc28"],"keyword":["game ai"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BB015CAA2810C88EB8802FBA3233F66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIG.2011.6031988","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorge","key":"muñozpau","last":"Muñoz","name":"Muñoz, Jorge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgios N.","key":"yannakakispau","last":"Yannakakis","name":"Yannakakis, Georgios N.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"0e2c06ee-d065-4477-93e1-d5ccf2f48fec","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","name_org":"Mulvey, Fiona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"German","key":"gutierrezpau","last":"Gutierrez","name":"Gutierrez, German","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Araceli","key":"sanchispau","last":"Sanchis","name":"Sanchis, Araceli","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2011.6031988","isbn":["9781457700095"],"pages":"47-54","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence and Games (CIG), 2011 IEEE Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054013729"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-494d4082-cae2-48c3-a993-7381c219cc28"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards gaze-controlled platform games","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382361","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Eye and gaze tracking have a long history but there is still plenty of room for further development. In this concluding chapter for Section 6, we consider future perspectives for the development of eye and gaze tracking.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Mardanbegi, Diako"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384042"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye tracking","Future Development","Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discussion and future directions for eye tracker development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84898560179","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384042","identifier":[{"id":"84898560179","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bdb10dd0-6a4a-49f8-bc24-b1c9ccb44449"],"keyword":["eye tracking","future development","methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DD13CA5B5DCCEA139ED318724FD3426F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona